  "Id": 2716,
  "Title": "SeeMe in Indiana, USA!",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Our star Simulation Education Analyst, Ms. Rahina Inayat Ali, represented the CIME Team virtually at the prestigious SimGHOSTS conference which took place in Fort Wayne, Indiana, United States.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClassCB2D612FDB5346BFA260A9B25CA78F8F\"><p>Our star Simulation Education Analyst, Ms. Rahina Inayat Ali, represented the CIME Team virtually at the prestigious SimGHOSTS conference which took place from the 3rd to the 6th of August 2021 in Fort Wayne, Indiana, United States.</p><p>She participated in a variety of activities and attended numerous lectures over the duration of the event. She also presented her own research about incorporating high fidelity simulation into medical school curricula, and how it may be used to replace traditional clinical rotations in fields such as Emergency Medicine. Her findings were deeply appreciated by audience, which included world leaders in the realm of clinical simulation.<br></p></div>",
